---
import DocsPage from "../../layouts/DocsPage.astro"

export const prerender = true
---

<DocsPage id="github">

          <p>
            Task in, pull request out. Run <code>vector github install</code> once inside a repository: it writes a
            workflow that installs the CLI from npm on every <code>/vector</code> comment, then add the
            <code>VECTOR_CLI_TOKEN</code> secret from your account page. From then on, commenting
            <code>/vector fix the flaky auth test</code> on an issue opens a branch and a pull request; commenting on an
            existing pull request replies on that branch.
          </p>
          <p>
            Every pull request carries its evidence, not just a diff: a Changes table with line counts per file, the
            output of any test, typecheck, lint, or build command the agent ran with its exit code, the measured token
            cost of the run, the judge's PASS or FAIL verdict when a judge pass ran, and a link back to the workflow run.
            Reviewers see what was checked before they read a line.
          </p>
          <h2>Connect a model for GitHub Actions</h2>
          <p>
            In 1.99.91, GitHub runs need your own provider credentials. The <code>VECTOR_CLI_TOKEN</code> secret
            authenticates your Vector account; it does not provide model access. Add the provider key as a repository
            secret and pass it into each job that calls Vector, using the provider's environment variable, such as
            <code>ANTHROPIC_API_KEY</code> or <code>OPENAI_API_KEY</code>. Set <code>MODEL</code> in the job's environment
            to a model that provider offers, in <code>provider/model</code> format.
          </p>
          <p>
            New workflows connect the selected provider's secret automatically. Check older workflows too: provider-key
            lines that are commented out do not pass the secret into the run.
            If no model is configured or available, Vector stops with setup instructions instead of selecting an
            unavailable model.
            Automatic reviews can use <code>REVIEW_AUTO_MODEL</code> to choose a separate model. See
            <a href="/docs/code-review">Vectorscope setup</a> for review controls.
          </p>
          <p class="note">
            Upcoming release: OpenCode-hosted providers will no longer be available, including access with your own
            OpenCode API key. Connect another provider for GitHub runs. This service change is implemented in source;
            the release version and installer publication are pending.
          </p>
          <p class="note">
            One repository setting is required: under Settings → Actions → General →
            Workflow permissions, tick "Allow GitHub Actions to create and approve pull requests" (GitHub leaves it off
            by default; without it the branch is pushed and Vector comments a compare link instead). Pull requests opened
            with the built-in GitHub token do not trigger the repository's other workflows; use a personal access token
            if you need CI to run on them.
          </p>
</DocsPage>
